## meta_effect

* Supported Scopes: any
* Supported Targets: THIS, ROOT, PREV, FROM, OWNER, CONTROLLER, OCCUPIED, CAPITAL

```
meta effects can be used for building effects from strings and running them. following example will give Germany 42 pp:
meta_effect = {
    text = {
        [COUNTRY] = {
            add_political_power = [POW]
        }
    }
    COUNTRY = "GER"
    POW = 42
    debug = no #set to yes if you want to see what game actually executes
}

```

meta_effect = {
	text = {
		create_wargoal = {
			type = take_state_focus
			target = event_target:independence_wave_reclamation_front_target
			generator = { [IW_RECLAMATION_STATE] }
			expire = [IW_RECLAMATION_EXPIRE]
		}
	}
	IW_RECLAMATION_STATE = "[independence_wave_reclamation_front_state.GetID]"
	IW_RECLAMATION_EXPIRE = "[?independence_wave_reclamation_front_expire_days|.0]"

# Apply caller-selected building damage in the current state through meta text.
# Required temporary inputs: dynamic_building_damage_type (building token),
# dynamic_building_damage_amount (number). Inputs are read-only and have no defaults.
damage_state_building_dynamic = {
	meta_effect = {
		text = {
			damage_building = {
				type = [BUILDING_TYPE]
				damage = [BUILDING_DAMAGE]
			}
		}
		BUILDING_TYPE = "[?dynamic_building_damage_type.GetTokenKey]"
		BUILDING_DAMAGE = "[?dynamic_building_damage_amount]"
	}
